    <statement><p>Find an equation of a plane containing the three points
(-3, 2, -4), (-1, -2, -1), (-1, -1, 1) in which the coefficient of <m>x</m> is -11.</p>
<p><fillin characters="60" name="AnSwEr0001"/> = 0.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-11\mathopen{}\left(x-\left(-3\right)\right)+\left(-4\right)\mathopen{}\left(y-2\right)+2\mathopen{}\left(z-\left(-4\right)\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
